% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display the original image, filtered image, and edge image
subplot(1,3,1), imshow(input_image); title('Original Image');
subplot(1,3,2), imshow(filtered_image); title('Filtered Image');
subplot(1,3,3), imshow(edge_image); title('Edge Image');
```
This modified code applies a Gaussian filter using the `fspecial` function and then filters the grayscale image using the `imfilter` function before performing edge detection with the Sobel operator. The resulting edge image will be less affected by noise due to the pre-processing Gaussian filter.

