 To make the circle element look more 3D, you can add some additional CSS properties such as a chamfer box-shadow and a rotation transformation. Here's an example of how you can modify the `.circle` class:

```css
.circle {
  fill: radial-gradient(white, lightblue);
  filter: drop-shadow(15px 15px 15px gray);
  transition: transform 0.3s ease-in-out;
  background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #fff, #ffcccc);
  box-shadow: 10px 10px 15px 0px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.75), 15px 15px 20px 0px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2), -15px -15px 20px 0px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
