response:
 Your implementation is a good start for finding unique words between two texts in MATLAB. To make it more efficient for handling large amounts of text, consider the following optimizations:
1. Use text scanning functions like `textscan` or `regexp` instead of reading the entire text into memory at once using `fileread`. These functions allow you to read data in smaller chunks.
2. Preallocate memory for `words1` and `words2` to improve performance.
3. Use a hash table or a set for faster set difference operation.

Here's an updated implementation based on your code:

```matlab
% Read text files line by line
fid1 = fopen('Text1.txt','r');
text1 = [];
while ~feof(fid1)
    line = fgetl(fid1);
    words1 = strsplit(lower(line),'\s+'); % Split words by whitespace
    text1 = [text1; words1]; % Concatenate with previous words
end
fclose(fid1);

fid2 = fopen('Text2.txt','r');
text2 = [];
while ~feof(fid2)
    line = fgetl(fid2);
    words2 = strsplit(lower(line),'\s+'); % Split words by whitespace
    text2 = [text2; words2]; % Concatenate with previous words
end
fclose(fid2);

% Find unique words in text1 that do not appear in text2
n = length(text1);
uniqueWords = cell(1, n);
for i = 1:n
    if ~ismember(text2{i}, uniqueWords)
        uniqueWords{end+1} = text1{i};
    end
end
% Print the unique words
disp(uniqueWords);
```

