However, if your texts are extremely large, consider using the Text Analytics Toolbox or Memory Mapped Files to improve efficiency. These methods allow you to work with large text data more efficiently by processing it in chunks rather than loading the entire content into memory at once.

The following example demonstrates how to use the Text Analytics Toolbox for finding unique words between two documents:

1. Install and add the Text Analytics Toolbox to your MATLAB path.
2. Use the `tokenizedDocument` function to create tokenized document objects for both texts.
3. Find the difference between the bags of words using the `bagOfWords` function and the `intersect` method.
4. Display the unique words.

```MATLAB
% Read text files
text1FileID = fopen('Text1.txt','r');
text1Data = textscan(text1FileID,'%s',Inf,'Delimiter','\n');
text1 = text1Data{1};
fclose(text1FileID);

text2FileID = fopen('Text2.txt','r');
text2Data = textscan(text2FileID,'%s',Inf,'Delimiter','\n');
text2 = text2Data{1};
fclose(text2FileID);

% Create tokenized document objects
documents = tokenizedDocument(lower(cell2mat(cats({text1}',2))));
documents2 = tokenizedDocument(lower(cell2mat(cats({text2}',2))));

% Find unique words
bag1 = bagOfWords(documents);
bag2 = bagOfWords(documents2);
uniqueWords = intersect(keys(bag1), keys(bag1) \ keys(bag2));

% Print the unique words
