 I'm here to help you resolve the issue you're encountering while performing a create mutation in Neo4j using GraphQL. The error message suggests that there's no registered procedure named `apoc.util.validate`. Here's how you can troubleshoot and potentially fix this problem:

1. Check if APOC library is installed:
APOC (Awesome Procedures On Cypher) is an open-source library of procedures and functions for Neo4j. Make sure you have installed it in your Neo4j instance. If not, follow these instructions to install it: https://github.com/neo4j-contrib/neo4j-apoc-procedures#installation

2. Verify APOC procedure availability:
You can check if the `apoc.util.validate` procedure is available by running the following query in your Neo4j Browser or any other Neo4j client:
```java
CALL apoc.help('apoc.util.validate') YIELD procedureName, signature, description
RETURN procedureName as ProcedureName, description as Description
```
If the result shows the procedure name and its description, then the problem might be related to your GraphQL setup. In that case, please check the next steps.

3. Configure GraphQL to use APOC:
To use APOC procedures in GraphQL, you need to configure Neo4j driver used by GraphQL to include the APOC library. For example, if you're using `neo4j-driver-core` in Node.js, add the following lines to your configuration file:
```javascript
const driver = neo4j.driver("bolt://localhost:7687", neo4j.auth.basic("neo4j", "password"));
driver.session().runTransaction((tx) => {
  tx.run(`LOAD_SCRIPT FROM 'file://path/to/apoc/3.5.1/apoc.neo4j.jar' AS script`);
  return tx.commit();
});

export default driver;
```
Replace `path/to/apoc/3.5.1/apoc.neo4j.jar` with the actual path to the APOC jar file on your system.

