 To retrieve the username from a JSON Web Token (JWT) in an ASP.NET C# WebApi project, you can follow these steps:

1. Install the `Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens` NuGet package if you haven't already. This package includes the necessary classes for working with JWT tokens.

```bash
Install-Package Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens
```

2. Create a method to validate and extract the username from the JWT token. Here's an example of how you might implement this method:

```csharp
using System;
using System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt;
using Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens;

public static string GetUsernameFromToken(string token)
{
    try
    {
        // Set up the signing key and validation parameters
        var signingKey = new SymmetricSecurityKey(Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes("your_secret_key"));
        var validationParameters = new TokenValidationParameters
        {
            ValidateIssuerSigningKey = true,
            IssuerSigningKey = signingKey,
            ValidateIssuer = false,
            ValidateAudience = false,
            ValidateLifetime = false
        };

        // Decode and validate the JWT token
        var handler = new JwtSecurityTokenHandler();
        var jwtToken = handler.ReadJwtTokenFromString(token);

        // Extract the username from the claims
        return jwtToken.Claims.FirstOrDefault(x => x.Type == "sub")?.Value;
    }
    catch (Exception ex)
    {
        throw new Exception("Invalid or expired token.", ex);
    }
}
```

Replace `"your_secret_key"` with your application's secret key used to sign the JWT tokens.

