 To auto-prefix a string before using it as a regular expression in JavaScript, you can use the `RegExp` constructor and concatenate the prefix to the regular expression pattern. Here's an example:

```javascript
const prefix = 'auto-'; // Define your prefix here
const regexPattern = /your_regex_pattern/; // Define your regex pattern here

// Auto-prefix the regex pattern with the prefix
const autoPrefixRegex = new RegExp(`${prefix}${regexPattern.source}`);

// Now you can use 'autoPrefixRegex' as your prefixed regex
console.log(autoPrefixRegex.test('some input string'));
```

