     _ => {
         if n % 2 == 0 {
             true
         } else {
             false
         }
     }
 }
}
```

This version of the function checks for specific cases using the `match` statement and uses an `if` condition for more general cases. The `|` operator is used in the `match` arm to check multiple values at once. This approach is more concise and idiomatic in Rust compared to the JavaScript code.

